From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] PinnerService: read the last used app's compiled code after boot

On PW3 the first start of an app after boot waits on the flash: the eMMC
reads about 27 MB/s at most (eMMC 4.5, DDR52 already), and starting WeRead
(compiled "speed", 115 MB odex and 71 MB vdex) faults in about 200 MB in
small pieces: 18-22 s to the reader page against 10 s with the files cached
(measured on PW3, 2026-10-15). Read in order beforehand, the same files take
5.6 s, and the start then takes 13-16 s.

PW3 boots into Android each time it is chosen from the Kindle library, and
the first thing opened is usually the app used last. With
ro.pw3.prefetch_recent_app, PinnerService reads, once boot has completed and on
a background thread, the .odex, .vdex and app image of the most recent task's
app other than home into the page cache. Nothing is locked (PinnerService's
pinning would hold 186 MB of a 512 MB device); the reads stop at half the
available memory; the time is logged.

Profile-guided layout (speed-profile, or speed with a profile and an app
image) was measured as well: speed-profile reads less (118 MB) but runs the
rest interpreted, 28 s cold and 18-22 s warm; 8.1's dexlayout does not reorder
compiled code, so with "speed" a cold start still reads 205 MB.

